  "comment": "**What it does**\nThe **full Minervini trend template** - pure price action, zero fundamentals, exactly as you asked.\n\n- **The stack** - price above the 50-day, 50 above 150, 150 above 200. Written as column-to-column comparisons, so it is the real stack and not a distance approximation.\n- **Near the highs** - within 25% of the 52-week high.\n- **Well off the lows** - at least 30% above the 52-week low.\n- **Leadership** - RS Rank 80+.\n- **Tradeable** - $300M+ and 100k average daily volume.\n\n**About the count**: this returns **335 names right now**. You said 'whatever the market gives', and that is what this is - the number rises in a broad advance and collapses in a correction. **Watching it shrink is itself a market signal.**\n\n**How to tweak**\n- **Want fewer, stronger names?** Raise `rs_rank` to 90. That is the sharpest single cut here (it took 737 down to 390 at 80).\n- **Want tighter to the highs?** Change `pct_from_52w_high` from -25 to -10 for names actually breaking out.\n- **Want bigger companies?** Raise `market_cap` to $2B.\n- **Note**: the classic template also wants the 200-day line itself to be RISING. We do not store that, so it is the one piece of the template missing here.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `rs_rank`** - the leadership measure, and the thesis.\n- **Tiebreak on `momentum_score`** - it blends RS with the MA distances and the 52-week-high gap.\n- **Avoid `value_score` and `quality_score`** - this screen deliberately ignores fundamentals, so ranking on them mixes in a thesis you excluded.\n- **Worth a look**: sort by `pct_from_52w_high` descending to find the names closest to breaking out.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find stocks in a confirmed strong uptrend \u2014 the full Minervini trend template,\npure price action, no fundamentals at all.\n- **Goal**: momentum. **Dividends / profits**: ignore completely \u2014 price only.\n- **The template**: price above the 50-day line; 50-day above 150-day above\n  200-day (the full stack); within 25% of the 52-week high; at least 30% above\n  the 52-week low; RS Rank 80+.\n- **Tradeable**: enough daily volume. **Size**: $300M and bigger.\n- **Kinds**: normal stocks only. **Risk**: volatile is fine \u2014 that is the game.\n- **Results**: whatever the market gives (~50-300 depending on conditions).\n- **Sorting**: RS Rank first, tiebreak momentum score.",
